breaking an antique item that changed  the future of cinema defending the  legacy of someone iconic being a victim  of a near fatal car crash these are just  a few of the challenges the stars of  quentin tarantino's iconic filmography  have had to overcome while filming keep  watching to find out quentin tarantino's  2015 film the hateful eight shares a  number of similarities with his debut  feature reservoir dogs one major detail  both films share is that for the most  part they each take place in one  location reservoir dogs sees a group of  strangers confined to a warehouse while  the hateful eight places the characters  in a stagecoach lodge while one might  imagine that a movie taking place  indoors for the majority of its run time  would be relatively straightforward to  film that was absolutely not the case  for the hateful eight as revealed by the  hollywood reporter tarantino demanded an  authentic environment rather than  shooting the interior shots in a studio  the director instead chose to place his  cast in colorado's sub-zero temperatures  for 10 weeks starting in january once  inside the lodge the director would  reportedly keep the single room at a 35  degree temperature to keep the  performances and the shivering realistic  actor walton goggins revealed that it  was so cold the cast and crew would  squeeze themselves under the set lights  for warmth thankfully the grueling time  on set led the film's stars to bond and  ultimately look forward to the end  result samuel jackson mentioned to  collider we were miserable in the  environment you could see our breath but  the stuff that we were doing was amazing  set in post civil war wyoming the  hateful eight follows eight strangers  cooped up in a stagecoach lodge while  they wait for a blizzard to subside  among the strangers is bounty hunter  john the hangman ruth played by kurt  russell and his prisoner daisy dahmergu  played by jennifer jason lee  unfortunately the duo found themselves  in a scene with painful real-life  consequences at one point in the film  dahmer ghoul sits in the lodge and plays  a guitar but her moment of peace is  swiftly interrupted by roof snatching it  away and smashing it to bits right next  to her music time's over  if you pay attention to lee's reaction  in the scene you'll see a look of sheer  panic and she wasn't hamming it up for  the camera as russell came to find out  the guitar he smashed was a genuine  antique from the 19th century borrowed  from the martin guitar museum according  to the film sound mixer mark ulano  russell was supposed to grab the guitar  and wait for the scene to cut while crew  members exchanged the priceless  instrument for a double according to  business insider these details were not  adequately explained to the actor the  museum director was horrified at the  destruction of the piece and although he  was reimbursed for the damages he  declared that the company wouldn't be  loaning out their guitars to film sets  anymore in 2016 lee told billboard that  russell felt so bad about the mix-up he  almost cried when he found out  for anyone who's seen 1992's reservoir  dogs it's almost impossible to listen to  the steelers real hit stuck in the  middle with you without immediately  thinking of michael madsen's mr blonde  grooving to the beat while mutilating a  police officer although madsen nailed  the part of the psychopathic mr blonde  he initially never saw his character as  the villain instead he figured the  audience would appreciate him hurting a  cop in a movie where all the  protagonists were criminals that is  until he learned one particular detail  about the officer according to tarantino  during rehearsals the director himself  played the role of the tortured police  officer at one point while in character  he blurted out that he had a child  madsen who had recently had a son felt  immediate discomfort knowing his  character was supposed to torture a  father changed his entire perception of  the scene madsen said he was also  intimidated to shoot his deranged dance  and almost refused to do it while matson  admits that reservoir dogs was important  in launching his career he believes his  now iconic role as mr blonde ruined his  chances of showing his acting range in  the years to come he told the hollywood  reporter unfortunately it typecasted me  as a bad guy i would prefer to be a  leading man  pulp fiction star uma thurman was once  one of quentin tarantino's most frequent  collaborators the pair had such a  professional love for one another that  tarantino called thurman his muse in a  2004 interview with rolling stone while  tarantino was quick to gush about his  leading lady in public things weren't  exactly as they seemed behind the scenes  as it turns out during the filming of  kill bill tarantino put thurman in an  incredibly dicey situation which she  didn't speak about until 2018. in a  shocking interview with the new york  times thurman detailed a story about a  scene that saw her driving a convertible  an issue arose after thurman spoke to  one of the crew members who suggested  the car might be unsafe to drive she  told tarantino she wanted a stunt person  to do it she explained to the times  quentin came in my trailer and didn't  like to hear no he was furious thurman  ultimately cooperated but the scene  nearly cost her her life in footage of  the incident that she published on her  instagram thurman loses control of the  vehicle and smashes into a tree the  accident damaged both her neck and her  knees and led to a massive argument with  tarantino the duo settled their  differences years later with tarantino  finally giving thurman the footage to  share with the public for years leading  up to this dispute he'd had it covered  up by disgraced producer harvey  weinstein  after once upon a time in hollywood came  out in 2019 quentin tarantino's  long-anticipated ninth feature film was  met with immediate backlash due to the  depiction of martial arts legend bruce  lee on camera during one scene lee  played by mike moe boasts that he could  beat cash's clay in a fight leading brad  pitt's character cliff boof to  laughingly disagree an enraged lee  challenges booth to a fight which ends  with each man getting knocked down over  the course of two rounds before someone  else intervenes according to the los  angeles times bruce lee's family  considered his depiction in the film a  mockery interestingly enough if  tarantino had it his way that mockery  would have gotten much worse according  to a huffington post interview with  stunt coordinator robert alonso the  original script saw booth winning a  third round against lee which didn't sit  well with the cast and crew including  brad pitt alonzo explained that pid  voiced his discomfort with the scene  adding that it was actually thanks to  the actors insistence that tarantino  changed the outcome according to mo  tarantino didn't mean any disrespect by  lee's portrayal in fact mo confirmed  that the director was a big fan of lee's  work he elaborated that at moe's  audition the pair spoke about the  martial arts icon for a solid half hour  quentin tarantino's 2012 spaghetti  western django unchained was met with  widespread criticism after its release  critics blasted the flick for its  jarring depictions of slavery a few  years before the civil war countless  racial slurs and its abundant violence  the film depicts django a freed slave  played by jamie foxx and german bounty  hunter dr king schultz played by  christoph vaults as they travel through  the south hunting criminals ultimately  the pair's journey leads them to try to  rescue django's wife groom hilda played  by kerry washington from a plantation  where she's held captive in an interview  with indie wire washington revealed her  initial hesitation to participate in the  movie due to the brutal on-screen  torture her characters subject to she  explained i was scared about the places  i had to go emotionally and  psychologically as an artist thankfully  she and fox had previously worked  together in the biopic ray and the  actors were able to lean on one another  throughout the taxing shoot washington  even recalled telling her co-star if  this movie goes on for one week longer  i'm not going to survive it ultimately  washington persevered even snagging a  best actress award from bet however it  wasn't easy washington told indie wire  that at one point during filming her  parents and manager came to set to  support her and one of the first things  washington did after returning home was  call her therapist  kerry washington wasn't the only actor  who had difficulty filming django  unchained while tarantino who was born  in the south told npr that he considered  the film a cultural catharsis filming  was difficult for a number of the  a-listers involved among them was  leonardo dicaprio who played despicable  plantation owner calvin candy the actor  revealed how difficult he found  portraying the inhumane character in a  chat with the screen actors guild  foundation it was really tough it was  actually uh  took a a long time to adjust to he never  quite felt  comfortable but that's part of what we  do you know dicaprio elaborated that his  co-stars were supportive he acknowledged  that in particular jamie foxx offered up  his own encouragement whenever candy did  something horrific and while fox had a  somewhat gentle approach to soothing  dicaprio's nerves fellow co-star samuel  jackson had a much more blunt way of  supporting the actor fox told indy wire  that one day jackson outright told  dicaprio to get over it reportedly  jackson's words stuck with dicaprio to  the point where when he came back to set  the next day he was completely in  character  1997's jackie brown is quentin  tarantino's most subtle film while the  director is usually known for  over-the-top flashiness in his visuals  and dialogue jackie brown takes a  reserved approach for going experimental  camera work and choosing to tell a more  gentle human story the film's  protagonist is jackie brown played by  pam greer a flight attendant who  smuggles cash for her gun runner boss  played by samuel jackson once the police  catch her they demand she cooperate with  them however the plucky lead has a plan  to keep the cash for herself filming  such an understated tarantino film may  sound easier than partaking in one of  his more violent epics but that doesn't  mean there wasn't at least one  uncomfortable moment on set as greer  revealed to peopletv's couchsurfing one  scene of the crime flick sees her  character holding a gun to jackson's  nether regions however insurance  policies would not allow greer to use a  weapon during rehearsals greer told  cinema blend she had to use her own hand  instead unsurprisingly this led to some  awkward interactions between the actors  and some accidental grazing of jackson's  groin after these uncomfortable moments  passed greer assured her co-star that  she'd be a lot more confident when the  time came to use an actual weapon anyone  who has seen the film will know she  absolutely delivered on that front  the late great lawrence tourney was  already a hollywood staple by the time  he starred in reservoir dogs according  to the hollywood reporter turning earned  his acting stripes being typecast as a  villain usually portraying mafiosos and  thieves reportedly his off-camera  persona wasn't particularly warm either  as the actor's star power grew he became  increasingly more temperamental as  tarantino told the guardian when he cast  tourney as crime boss joe cabot in 1992  his first few weeks of shooting were  pure torture tarantino who's certainly  not renowned for his etiquette on set  went so far as to call tourney a  complete lunatic when filming for  reservoir dogs began the director opted  to shoot tourney's scenes in the first  week after a stressful week of filming  the actor and director's conflict came  to a violent head tarantino explained by  the end of the week everybody on set  hated tourney it wasn't just me and in  the last 20 minutes of the first week we  had a blowout and got into a fistfight i  fired him and the whole crew burst into  applause although the thin newbie  director thought that getting rid of  tourney would ruin his chances at a big  break in hollywood he fortunately had  the movie's biggest star on his side  harvey keitel assured the studio that  everything would turn out fine and the  rest is history uma thurman and john  travolta's dance scene in pulp fiction  remains one of the most iconic moments  in 90 cinema as explained by the daily  beast the scene was inspired by jean-luc  goddard's 1964 classic bond depart  reportedly tarantino has always been  inspired by the way goddard incorporated  music and dance into his films most of  the scene was improvised and travolta  didn't seem to have many issues with it  but the same can't be said for thurman  despite her character's on-screen  enthusiasm now i want to dance i want to  win  i want that trophy  so that's good thurman told variety i  was more afraid of the dancing than  almost anything because it was exactly  to my total insecurity thurman credited  her youth and lanky build as the  culprits behind her timothy thankfully  she added once the dancing actually  began she adored the experience in a  funny and heartfelt moment at the 2022  academy awards thurman and travolta took  to the stage alongside samuel l jackson  to celebrate the film's 28th anniversary  the two actors briefly recreated their  legendary dance with thurman quipping  maybe later we'll have a five dollar  milkshake  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  quentin tarantino films are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one

